.DS_Store
.build/
build/
dist/
DerivedData/
*.xcodeproj
*.xcworkspace
.swiftpm/
.env
node_modules/
mcp-server/dist/
mcp-server/dist-test/
*.log
assets/generated/

# On-device speech model weights (m23-n1). ~1.5 GB of CoreML `.mlmodelc`
# bundles + a HuggingFace tokenizer, copied in from a local source — NEVER
# committed. Root-anchored so it can only ever match the one directory
# `WhisperModelLocation.relativeModelsPath` names; scripts/bundle.sh (m23-n3)
# copies that same directory inside the codesign seal.
/Models/
# HuggingFace snapshot bookkeeping that rides along next to a copied
# tokenizer (`tokenizer/.cache/huggingface`). Belt-and-braces: the copy step
# already excludes it, this makes staging it impossible.
**/.cache/huggingface/

# Python bytecode from the gate-analysis helpers (`scripts/gates/_*.py`).
# Build output, never source: regenerated on every run of the tool that
# imports them.
__pycache__/

# Compiled gate helper (m20-d). Build output of the committed
# `scripts/gates/m20d-bhrate.swift`; the gate rebuilds it on demand and aborts
# with the swiftc line if it is missing.
/scripts/gates/m20d-bhrate

# Per-gate coverage baseline (m23-ep-3). LOCAL RUN STATE, not a shared artifact:
# it records that a gate ran *on this machine* (`ranAt`) alongside the gate
# file's content hash. Checking it in would report CURRENT on a fresh checkout
# for gates that never ran there — a false green, which is the exact defect
# class this milestone exists to remove. It also rewrites on every single gate
# invocation, so tracking it would churn the diff constantly.
/scripts/gate-corpus-baseline.json

# Append-only history of every baseline write (m25-q), sibling to the file
# above and gitignored for the same reason: it is LOCAL RUN STATE, and a
# tracked history would conflict on every gate run across this repo's
# concurrent sessions. Unlike the baseline itself, this is never rewritten —
# it grows — so keeping it out of git isn't about diff churn, it's the same
# "this describes THIS machine's runs" reasoning as the baseline.
/scripts/gate-corpus-baseline.json.history.jsonl

# Film-pipeline build intermediates. assemble.py's --work defaults to a
# RELATIVE "segments", so it lands wherever the builder happened to be standing
# -- twice already that was inside this repo (102 MB at the root, more under
# scripts/video). They are regenerable output, never source.
segments/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- media
# ⚠ USER RULE 2026-09-04: NEVER COMMIT A GENERATED VIDEO. Only the tools that
# make them belong in git -- the films themselves are regenerable output and
# are measured in tens of megabytes each. These patterns are deliberately
# broad and are placed LAST so a genuinely needed asset can be re-admitted
# with an explicit negative rule below, rather than by weakening them.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.m4v
*.webm
*.wav
*.aiff
*.flac
*.dmg
*.zip

# The kit's own committed assets, re-admitted explicitly. These are SOURCE:
# design-voice.py needs the reference voice, and the films cannot be rebuilt
# on another machine without it.
!plugins/narrated-film/assets/reference-voice.wav
!plugins/narrated-film/assets/reference-voice.mp3
!claude-plugin/skills/demo-film/assets/reference-voice.wav
!claude-plugin/skills/demo-film/assets/reference-voice.mp3

# Captured UI stills and rendered cards: output of a filming run, thousands of
# frames, regenerated by re-running the capture.
shots/
vo/

# Emitted film/Shorts specs — generated by scripts/video/session/spec.py and
# shorts.py from MEASUREMENTS.json. They embed absolute paths to shot and audio
# directories that are themselves gitignored, so a committed copy is wrong the
# moment anyone else runs it.
/scripts/video/session/F1.json
/scripts/video/comp/B3.json
/scripts/video/session/V?.json

# Frame BURSTS and manim/ffmpeg intermediates from the lesson films. Every one
# of these is regenerated by re-running bursts.py; the mono-bass pilot alone is
# 499 MB of bursts/ and 546 MB of out/, and only *.mp4 and *.wav in there were
# caught by the patterns above -- the PNG frames were not.
bursts/
/scripts/video/lessons/*/manim/
/scripts/video/lessons/*/out/
/scripts/video/lessons/*/media/

# The same rule as `bursts/` above, for the Shorts and series films, which use
# `out/` rather than `bursts/`: rendered frames, per-segment meter strips and
# payload JSON, all regenerated by re-running the build. MEASURED 2026-09-15:
# 43 682 untracked images under scripts/video/shorts alone, 50 GB in `roads/`
# and `tunes/` -- none of it source, and it drowns `git status` (45 222 entries)
# so real untracked work cannot be seen.
/scripts/video/shorts/*/*/out/
/scripts/video/series/*/out/
/scripts/video/comp/out/
/scripts/video/comp/media/
# The M39 features demo (2026-09-21): same rule again. `features/out/` holds the
# narrated film, three 2-minute renders, six visualiser videos, 33 stills per
# variant and the narration takes -- 274 MB, all of it regenerated by re-running
# build.mjs -> measure.py -> make-viz.sh -> narrate.py -> assemble.py.
/scripts/video/features/out/
# The released tree was copied out of the session scratchpad on 2026-09-21 so it
# would survive the session -- which also brought its build scratch (`work/` is
# per-stage ffmpeg concat lists and meter dumps) and the pre-release cut, kept
# under `out-superseded-*` rather than deleted so the two are never confused.
# The broad *.wav/*.mp4/image rules below already cover the payload; these catch
# the small .txt/.json intermediates that would otherwise read as source.
/scripts/video/features/work/
/scripts/video/features/out-superseded-*/
# Pillow lives in a venv beside viz.py; viz.py recreates it on demand.
/scripts/video/features/viz/.venv/
# Staging app run state. Kept beside the scripts so the pid stays identifiable
# after the scratchpad is reaped -- a listener on 17695 with no pidfile means
# you do not know whose process it is, and kills here are pidfile-exact only.
/scripts/video/features/staging.json

# Emitted per-variant Shorts specs (246 files, 27 MB): the same generated-spec
# reasoning as the F1/B3/V? rules above, one file per variant trial.
/scripts/video/shorts/*/_variants/

# A DAW Pro profile the lesson build drives headlessly, autosave bundle and all.
# App run state, never source.
/scripts/video/lessons/out/

# Every IMAGE under scripts/video is generated: rendered stills, measurement
# ladders, contact strips, manim SVGs. MEASURED 2026-09-15 on the untracked set
# after the directory rules above -- 391 files, 200 MB, still nothing but
# output, in per-trial `measure/`, `strips/` and `stills/` directories that no
# directory pattern predicts. The SOURCE side of the same set is 468 files of
# py/json/mjs/txt/md/sh and NOT ONE IMAGE, which is what makes an
# extension rule the honest one here rather than a guess at more directories.
# A genuinely needed image can be re-admitted with an explicit negative rule.
/scripts/video/**/*.png
/scripts/video/**/*.jpg
/scripts/video/**/*.jpeg
/scripts/video/**/*.svg

# The last of the generated stragglers, each CHECKED rather than guessed at:
# `out-w2/`/`out-w3/` are width-variant siblings of the `out/` rule above;
# `screenrec` is a Mach-O arm64 binary sitting next to its own committed
# `screenrec.swift`; `.npz` are zipped numpy analysis caches; `.orig` is an
# editor backup; `.port` is staging run state; `_r*tmp/` is a scratch dir.
/scripts/video/**/out-w*/
/scripts/video/screenrec/screenrec
/scripts/video/**/_r*tmp/
*.npz
*.orig
*.port
*.pid
*.bak

# YouTube OAuth — never commit
scripts/video/publish/client_secret.json
scripts/video/publish/token.json

# Demo-render harness output (scripts/demos/render-variants.mjs): rendered
# .wav variants + manifest.json for a listen-later review set. Regenerable
# from the spec + the tree at render time; *.wav is already caught above but
# manifest.json and any staging-mode .dawproj are not, so this is explicit.
/scripts/demos/out/

.venv/

# p2-sing-d3 (W7-SD3, 2026-09-27): the two bundled singing guides are SOURCE assets, not output. They are app
# resources, regenerated byte-identically by SingGuideLine's generator (sha256 pinned in SingGuideFileGateTests).
# Without them a fresh checkout ships no guides, and the guide-leak check silently reports `measured: false`.
!Sources/DAWCore/Resources/BundledSamples/sing-guides/row-guide-high.wav
!Sources/DAWCore/Resources/BundledSamples/sing-guides/row-guide-low.wav
